---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="AI410 | AI, explained like you're 10">
  <header class="masthead home-hero">
    <div class="home-stage" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="orbit orbit-a"></span>
      <span class="orbit orbit-b"></span>
      <span class="orbit orbit-c"></span>
      <span class="scrap scrap-num scrap-1 float-a">05</span>
      <span class="scrap scrap-num scrap-2 float-b">06</span>
      <span class="scrap scrap-sticky scrap-3 float-c">10</span>
      <span class="scrap scrap-4 float-d">MCP</span>
      <span class="scrap scrap-5 float-e">the building</span>
      <img class="scrap scrap-stamp scrap-6 float-f" src="/images/ai410-mark.svg" alt="" width="56" height="56" />
      <span class="doodle doodle-star">★</span>
      <span class="doodle doodle-star doodle-star-2">★</span>
      <svg class="doodle doodle-scribble" viewBox="0 0 120 36" fill="none">
        <path d="M4 22c18-16 28 14 46 2 16-10 22 12 42-4 12-10 22 6 24 8" />
      </svg>
    </div>
    <p class="kicker reveal">Notes</p>
    <h1 class="reveal delay-1">AI, explained like you're <span class="flip">10</span>.</h1>
    <p class="byline reveal delay-2">By <a href="/who/">Adler Archer</a></p>
    <p class="dek reveal delay-3">I work around this subject and still get stuck on the jargon. I used to paste the words into a chat and ask it to explain them like I was 10. These pages are that habit, written down, with the usual terms next to the small ones.</p>
    <p class="home-go reveal delay-4">
      <a href="/lessons/">Lessons</a>
    </p>
  </header>
</Base>
